From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Pin yarn compressionLevel for reproducible offline cache

Must apply after the CVE patches (grafana-nanoid-cve.patch,
grafana-axios-cve.patch, grafana-browserslist-cve.patch): those
patches also bump entries in yarn.lock, and this patch's checksum
regeneration below must reflect their post-patch checksums, not the
pristine ones.

--- a/.yarnrc.yml
+++ b/.yarnrc.yml
@@ -2,7 +2,15 @@
 # It is a security risk that would allow arbitrary code execution both locally and in CI.
 # https://yarnpkg.com/configuration/yarnrc#approvedGitRepositories
 
-compressionLevel: mixed
+# Fixed (not upstream's "mixed") so the offline cache tarball gorget builds
+# from .yarn/cache is byte-reproducible: "mixed" lets yarn choose a
+# per-package compression level, which isn't guaranteed stable across
+# separate install runs even for identical resolved content. Applied after
+# the CVE/test patches (not as part of grafana-yarn-cache.patch) since
+# changing it requires yarn to regenerate every package's checksum in
+# yarn.lock (below) to match -- doing that before those patches would break
+# their ability to apply against the original checksums.
+compressionLevel: 0
 
 enableGlobalCache: false
 
--- a/yarn.lock
+++ b/yarn.lock
@@ -3,19 +3,19 @@
 
 __metadata:
   version: 10
-  cacheKey: 10
+  cacheKey: 10c0
 
